            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0410" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edgar</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-24T12:00:00+08:00">October 24,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 24—1:43 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>606. China Customs [head] L. K. Little, having transferred headquarters here, had
                    long talk Generalissimo latter’s request—who, although claiming unofficial
                    status, proceeded give orders. Generalissimo seriously worried over danger
                    invasion Formosa and wants customs boat for defense.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edgar</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
